      <h3>Which of these is actually free to start?</h3>
      <p>
        Three of the four. Kit (up to 10,000 subscribers, no automations), Beehiiv (up to 2,500, no monetisation features) and MailerLite (up to 250, automations included) all have permanent free plans with no credit card required. ActiveCampaign has a 14-day trial only.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>When will I be forced to pay?</h3>
      <p>
        At the moment you need the thing each free plan withholds: automation on Kit ($39/mo), monetisation on Beehiiv ($49/mo), subscriber #251 on MailerLite ($12/mo) — or day 15 on ActiveCampaign ($15/mo). Plan for the withholding, not the headline price.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>Which tool has the best deliverability?</h3>
      <p>
        All four are established senders with proper infrastructure, and no honest comparison can crown one from pricing pages. Beginners land in spam because of list quality, missing domain authentication and sudden volume — all within your control on any of these platforms. Pick on fit and billing rules; keep your list clean.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>Can I switch later without losing my subscribers?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes — your list exports as a CSV from all four, and Kit offers a free done-for-you migration on paid plans. What does <strong>not</strong> move is the plumbing: forms, landing pages, automations and sequences must be rebuilt in the new tool. That rebuild cost, not the subscription, is why the first choice matters.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What if I also want to sell a course or run funnels?</h3>
      <p>
        Then you are outside what these four are for. Either stack a separate tool (and pay the "tool tax" our <a href="/blog/systeme-io-review">Systeme.io review</a> breaks down) or start with an all-in-one whose free plan already includes funnels, a course and checkout.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="bottom-line">Bottom Line</h2>
  <p>
    For a beginner, the decision is not "which tool is best" but "which paywall do I want to meet first." Kit makes you pay for automation and gives you the longest free runway to reach it. MailerLite makes you pay for audience size and gives you automation from day one. Beehiiv makes you pay for monetisation and gives you a growth engine in exchange. ActiveCampaign makes you pay from day one — for everyone on your list, including the people who left — and gives you the deepest automation of the four when you grow into it.
  </p>
  <p>
